# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Nutrition Coach local runtime configuration — for the developer's machine only.
#
# This file is gitignored when copied to `.env` (`.gitignore` keeps `.env` and
# `.env.*` out of the repo; `.dockerignore` keeps them out of the build
# context). Copy it from `.env.example` and fill in your own values.
#
# NO SECRETS GO HERE. Not an API key, not a token. Anything that becomes a
# `VITE_*` value is COMPILED INTO the web bundle, which anyone who can load the
# app can read. `scripts/run_local_web.sh` reads this file as data (it is never
# executed), uses only the name below, and ignores — with a notice — anything
# that looks like a secret. Your BYOK API key is typed into Settings → Your AI at
# run time and kept inside the encrypted store.
#
# All variables are optional.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dev-only: use the in-memory store so the capture → log → Today loop works in
# the browser without the passphrase flow (the Vite dev server only: a release
# build has no such store, `tools/check_no_dev_store_in_build.sh`). Data lives and
# dies with the tab, and the app shows a visible DEV banner.
AI_NUTRITION_COACH_DEV_IN_MEMORY_STORE=true
